20e-5ce3-b17e-0ab4001a9339" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498698 1074 "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0),B(-2,-2)$ and $C(2,-8).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (0) & =-2(-3)-4 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-2) & =-2(-2)-4 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-8) & =-2(2)-4 \\\\ -8 & =-8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line." 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498699 1080 "$C$ only" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498699 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498699 1083 #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498700 1080 "$C$ only" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498700 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498700 1083 #uuid "a8f856d5-e5e8-54b8-ab43-051a8533362c" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498701 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498680 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498701 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498701 1071 "![](images/21/210db4ba3df7f9004c6ffe53336ce3e42d4156841560813478c404353b204c0c.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-4x+1?$" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498701 1072 #uuid "ac37c3c8-b208-5c81-a00d-e1bd9d503cf5" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498701 1074 "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,3),B(1,-1)$ and $C(2,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (3) & =-4(0)+1 \\\\ 3 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-1) & =-4(1)+1 \\\\ -1 & =-3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-7) & =-4(2)+1 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line." 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498702 1080 "$C$ only" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498702 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498702 1083 #uuid "aef1cd6c-325f-57b3-b55a-22367510cec4" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498703 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498694 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498703 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498703 1071 "![](images/1a/1aa0849898f763eedd84d050a7bd7c24bbb10c8f89c81e3f533622252330814e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+4.$" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498703 1072 #uuid "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498703 1074 "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-5)$, $B(1,5)$ and $C(2,10).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (-5) & =3(-3)+4 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+4 \\\\ 5 & =7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,10)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (10) & =3(2)+4 \\\\ 10 & =10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line." 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498704 1080 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498704 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498704 1083 #uuid "b31cf4f4-e928-5d0a-810e-cf15a16aed3f" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498705 1080 "$B$ only" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498705 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498705 1083 #uuid "b7497970-afdd-59b5-8946-7e774cc44e0c" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498706 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498692 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498706 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498706 1071 "![](images/1f/1ff37e7ea63a62de2a1ccbf59c53225b739be305f9e87f7aceca7735ba210bbd.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-3x?$" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498706 1072 #uuid "bbacf92b-66e8-58cd-bc32-e7d565177fbf" 13194139535342 17592186045443 true] [17592186498706 1074 "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,8),B(0,-2)$ and $C(2,-6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,8)$ results in a